{
  "$comment": "The order each release lists its drawings in, read off the Figma Changelog page on 9 Sep 2026 and pinned here so the site and the Paper board print the same sequence. Some entries are hand-ordered by family (0.6.0 opens on the singles and walks the money through its bases and circled halves) and some are plain alphabetical; which is which is the design file's call, not this file's. A name missing from a version's list is not dropped: build-history.mjs appends it in its own order and says so, so an entry can never publish fewer drawings than the release contained. 0.3.0 is deliberately absent: that entry adds no drawings, and the row of thirty under it is the sharp sample, which is named in lib/changelog.ts and already matches. The order also picks a release's cover: the site, the Paper board and the Figma card deal it one category at a time from this list, so 2.0.0 is pinned for its cover alone (18 Oct 2026, six drawings off it: a mark too small to read at that size, two mirror halves of drawings already there, a third big arrow beside two, and two part-filled chevron levels, which deal last so the category shows only its full ones). 2.1.0 is pinned the same way (20 Oct 2026): each category leads with a drawing that reads at cover size, so the cover shows the plain sigma, pi and lambda rather than their boxed forms, one of each mirrored pair of flips and symmetries, and the gripper beside the compass; Files deals last, so its third copy stays off. Read by pipeline/build-history.mjs.",
